        </svg>
        {t.scienceTitle}
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">{t.scienceSub}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs">
      <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900/80 p-4 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-300">1. Two-Fluid Atomization & Sauter Mean Diameter (D32)</h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded bg-slate-950 font-mono text-[11px] text-amber-200 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-800">
          D32 = (A / ALR^0.55) &times; [&sigma;_L / (&rho;_air &times; v_rel^2)]^0.45 &times; [1 + &mu;_L^2 / (&sigma;_L &times; &rho;_L &times; D_0)]^0.1
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Where ALR is the Air-to-Liquid mass ratio, &sigma;_L is binder surface tension (mN/m), and v_rel is the sonic relative exit velocity of the atomizing air jet. Increasing atomization air pressure expands sonic shear, reducing droplet size to prevent bed collapse.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900/80 p-4 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-300">2. Ergun Fluidization & Minimum Velocity (U_mf)</h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded bg-slate-950 font-mono text-[11px] text-amber-200 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-800">
          &Delta;P / L = 150 &times; [&mu;_g &times; (1 - &epsilon;)^2 / (&epsilon;^3 &times; d_p^2)] &times; U_g + 1.75 &times; [&rho;_g &times; (1 - &epsilon;) / (&epsilon;^3 &times; d_p)] &times; U_g^2
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Minimum fluidization velocity (U_mf) marks the transition where upward aerodynamic drag equals powder buoyant gravitational force. Superficial velocity U_g must operate within 2.0 to 4.5 &times; U_mf to maintain uniform bubbling fluidization.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900/80 p-4 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-300">3. NFPA 68 Deflagration Venting & Reduced Pressure (P_red)</h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded bg-slate-950 font-mono text-[11px] text-amber-200 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-800">
          A_v = C &times; A_s &times; [P_max / P_red - 1]^0.5 &times; (K_st / 100) &times; [1 + 1.75 &times; (P_stat - 0.1)]
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Determines the mandatory rupture panel vent area (A_v) required to relieve internal combustible dust explosion overpressure. P_red must remain strictly below the vessel yield design strength (P_vessel) to prevent fatal room bursting.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg bg-slate-900/80 p-4 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-300">4. Electrostatic Spark Discharge Energy & MIE Criterion</h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded bg-slate-950 font-mono text-[11px] text-amber-200 overflow-x-auto border border-slate-800">
          E_spark = 0.5 &times; C_isolated &times; V^2 &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; V = I_streaming &times; R_ground
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Pneumatic powder conveying generates streaming currents (I &approx; 10 to 100 &mu;A). If grounding resistance R_ground exceeds 10 Ohms, filter cages charge to thousands of volts, storing spark energies that exceed powder MIE (&lt;25 mJ), triggering ignition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

